hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"139","Ali bin Khashram told us, Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zinad, who is Abdullah bin Dhakwan, on the authority of Al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was informed of it. H Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala’ and Sa’id bin Abdul-Rahman narrated to us, saying: Sufyan, who is Ibn Uyaynah, narrated to us with this chain of transmission, saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Were it not that I would make it difficult for my nation, I would have ordered them to delay the evening meal and to use the siwak at every prayer.” Al-Makhzoumi did not confirm the delay of dinner."
"140","On the authority of Ali bin Ma’bad, on the authority of Ruh bin Ubadah, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Humaid bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If it were not that I would make it difficult for my nation, I would have ordered them to use the siwak with every ablution.” Abu Bakr said: This narration is in Al-Muwatta’, on the authority of Abu Hurairah: “If it were not that it would be difficult for his nation, he would have ordered them to use the siwak at every ablution.” It was narrated by Al-Shafi’i and Bishr bin Omar as the narration of a soul."
